{% section #step-2 step=2 title="Add the MCP server" %}

Connect the Appwrite MCP server to [Pi](https://pi.dev), a terminal coding agent, for deeper integration with the Appwrite API and documentation. It is a remote HTTP server, so you don't run a server on your machine.

If you don't have Pi yet, install it from your terminal on macOS or Linux. On Windows, or to install with npm, see [pi.dev](https://pi.dev).

```bash
curl -fsSL https://pi.dev/install.sh | sh
```

Pi connects to the server through [pi-mcp-adapter](https://github.com/nicobailon/pi-mcp-adapter), a Pi extension that adds MCP servers to your sessions. Install it:

```bash
pi install npm:pi-mcp-adapter
```

Add the Appwrite MCP server to `~/.pi/agent/mcp-adapter.json`. Create the file if it doesn't exist, or merge this into it:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "appwrite": {
      "url": "https://mcp.appwrite.io/",
      "auth": "oauth"
    }
  }
}
```

The server uses OAuth for authentication. Start Pi by running `pi` in your terminal, then run `/mcp-auth appwrite`. Your browser opens so you can sign in to your Appwrite account and authorize access. You don't need an API key. The adapter keeps the sign-in in your operating system's credential store.

{% info title="Pi's built-in MCP support" %}

Pi also has built-in MCP support, which you set up with `pi mcp add`. The events extension in [Step 4](#step-4) needs pi-mcp-adapter, so this guide uses the adapter. The adapter turns off the built-in support in Pi's settings and reads the servers you added with `pi mcp add`, so those keep working.

{% /info %}

{% /section %}

{% section #step-3 step=3 title="Test the integration" %}

Run `/mcp` in Pi to check that **appwrite** is listed with its tools. Then try out the following example prompts:

**Example prompts:**

- `Create a new user in my Appwrite project`
- `List all databases in my project`
- `Show me the tables in my database`
- `How do I set up real-time subscriptions in Appwrite?`
- `Show me how to authenticate users with OAuth`
- `How do I implement file uploads with Appwrite Storage?`

The following screenshot shows Pi answering `List the users in my Appwrite project pi-guide` for a test project.

